  "query_preview": "..\n(Tonight through next Monday)\nIssued at 1039 PM CDT Mon Aug 10 2026\n\nWarm conditions continue this evening as a heat wave shifts into\nhigh gear across much of the central and southern CONUS. The main\nfeature responsible is an amplifying ridge that will span much of\nthe Southern CONUS in the coming days with 594 dm heights over\nthe region by Tuesday afternoon. As such, highs Tuesday are\nexpected to be in the 90s with heat indices well above 100 F.\nPortions of the region, especially with westward extent towards\nthe Mississippi River, will experience afternoon heat indices\nbetween 105 - 109 F, prompting a Heat Advisory for these areas.\nSome potential exists for afternoon convection across portions of\nnorthern Mississippi and West Tennessee near the Tennessee River\nValley. However, convective coverage appears to be low at this\ntime, which will decrease the level of cooling for these areas.\nAny showers or storms will only be capable of locally gusty winds\nand heavy downpours through sunset.\n\nThe ridging will slightly weaken on Wednesday as an area of low-\namplitude troughing makes its way south from the Midwest.\nHowever, models indicate that its presence will be insufficient\nto promote both cooler temperatures and precipitation. Highs will\nstill reach into the 90s, approaching 100 across portions of\neastern Arkansas, with heat indices well above 100 across the\nentire region. Areas near and to the west of the Mississippi\nRiver will have heat index values potentially approaching 110 F.\nWith the absence of precipitation, heat products will be needed\nfor much of the Mid-South again on Wednesday.\n\nThe rest of the week follows a similar trend with the ridging\nreturning and scorching heat continuing to plague the southern\nCONUS. PoPs drop off precipitously, eventually nearing zero by\nThursday which lasts through this weekend. Therefore, no\nappreciable cooling or relief is expected and heat products are\nexpected to be needed for much, if not all, of the Mid-South by\nthe end of the week. Looking forward to next week also doesn't\nyield promising signs of cooling with ensembles favoring the\nexistence of the ridge through at least Tuesday. So, expect the\nheat to stick around and remember to stay hydrated and take\nfrequent breaks from exposure to the sun!",
